    "title": "Colorado Rockies vs. Los Angeles Dodgers game to air free on KTVD Friday",
    "text": "During a Colorado Rockies game, Josh Tartler, juggling his 15-month-old daughter, caught a foul ball one-handed, earning cheers from the crowd and announcers. DENVER — A Colorado Rockies fan became an instant crowd favorite Saturday when he caught a foul ball with one hand while cradling his 15-month-old daughter during the Rockies' game against the Los Angeles Dodgers. Josh Tartler was attending the game with his family when Dodgers slugger Teoscar Hernández fouled a pitch directly toward him. With no time to think, Tartler instinctively secured the ball using his elbow and body while keeping his infant daughter, Porter, safe in his arms. \"It was pretty reactionary,\" Tartler said. \"It was so direct at me that it would have been like stopping a bullet, so I decided to play it into my body.\" Tartler said the moment didn't fully register until he heard the crowd's reaction. \"After I caught it, I didn't think anything of it. I just kind of held it up, and then I could hear the crowd around me kind of erupting, and that's when I was like, oh, I see what they're doing.\" Rockies announcers called it the \"play of the day.\" Both father and daughter were uninjured. Tartler's connection to the Rockies runs deep — his father purchased season tickets during the franchise's first year in Denver.",
